WEBVTT

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.160
"Planet Shummoor
Day 26 of being lost in space"

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.660
"Planet Shummoor
Day 26 of being lost in space"
Wow, so Yunhua's singing was that good?

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:23.660
Oh, yes. I've never heard
anything so beautiful.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:29.290
It was so relaxing.
Not just mentally but physically, too.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.750
Yunhua's song was really the lifeline
that helped us make it through.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.620
That song really saved us all. Thank you.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.540
Oh, um...

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:44.290
Kanata, did you know Yunhua
wants to become a singer?

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.660
Oh, yeah.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.370
Yunhua is Lucy Lum's daughter.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.580
Lu...

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.540
Lucy Lum's daughter?!

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.290
Huh? That superstar singer?

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.330
Seriously?

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.660
W-W-W-W-W-Wait...

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.540
I guess there's a similarity if I look closely...

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.830
Also, she's mega cute...

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.290
Please don't stare!

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.750
Yunhua.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.950
Don't be so shy.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.580
There's no shame in self-expression.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.540
Yes.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.660
Like Aries said...

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:32.120
I'm enjoying this trip a little.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.620
Being on an adventure with everyone...

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.450
I can feel that way because...

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.910
...all of you are so warm and reliable.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:54.660
Singing is the only unique thing I can do,
but I'll do everything I can to help.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.660
Let's get home together,
through this adventure!

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.910
Aye, yeah!

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.750
Team B5 camp log.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.160
"Planet Shummoor
Day 27 of being lost in space"

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.830
"Planet Shummoor
Day 27 of being lost in space"
The search for food was not easy.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.290
Yum, yum, yummy!

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.250
I knew it!

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.330
Seriously?!

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:21.790
But then, Charce discovered that
the Pole Trees were edible.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:27.040
I figured if the Pole Trees are giant mushrooms,
not trees, maybe they're edible.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.450
Yes, it does look tasty.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.370
Aries, you and I are on the same page.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.120
Perhaps we were parent
and child in a previous life.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.540
Weirdo curiosity monsters...

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:43.870
We were able to resupply and
leave Shummoor after a five-day stay.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:50.330
--Goodbye!
--Goodbye!

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.790
We won't forget you, Gruppies!

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:59.790
They are so attached
to those unknown life forms.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.000
They helped us a lot.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:06.000
The experience at Shummoor was quite rough,

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.200
but I think it made us stronger.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.040
Luca...

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.040
I need a favor.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.450
Um...

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.410
Please don't stare.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.950
Are all boys idiots?!

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:46.040
Then a beef took my bag
and I was like, "Oh no!"

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.450
But someone named
Kanata Daibamomo helped me.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:54.080
He got one-two-one-two'ed, but announced
his candidacy to become champion...

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.620
Hey, we're descending soon.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.330
Everyone get to their seats!

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:01.040
Okay, I'll send another message tomorrow.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.660
I'll make sure to keep a log
every day. See you!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:19.290
"Aries's mother
Emma Spring"

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.500
Nine students from Caird High are missing.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:28.540
It has been almost 40 days since
they were last seen on Planet McPa.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:33.160
This unprecedented incident, where all
of the students on the camping trip

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.120
went missing, along with their luggage,
with no evidence of their whereabouts...

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.540
Aries...

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.910
"Caird High School
Day 49 of being lost in space"

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:47.700
Thank you all for coming today.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:54.200
I understand how difficult
this is for all of you.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.160
My son is one of the missing children.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:59.330
"Caird High School vice-principal
Ulgar's father
Gert Zweig"
My son is one of the missing children.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:07.950
As you must be aware, one month has passed
since the search was officially suspended.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:12.540
The time has come for us to accept the truth.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.040
We must file for a judicial
declaration of disappearance.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.410
Declaration of disappearance?

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:21.660
You want them declared legally dead?

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.410
Please wait! You're giving up?!

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:27.000
I'm not ready for that yet!

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.250
I understand how you must feel.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:34.040
But they can't remain missing forever.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:38.370
But... What about the rest of you?!

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:42.120
"Zack's father
Jed Walker"
We did everything we could
to continue the search.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:46.410
There's simply nothing more we can do.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.500
I have no reason to oppose.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:54.080
We have to start taking a more
realistic stance to these discussions.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:59.120
"Yunhua's mother
Wei Lu (Lucy Lum)"
Do you think your daughter will pop up
out of nowhere if you just keep believing?

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.120
Do you think your daughter will pop up
out of nowhere if you just keep believing?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.540
No, I...

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.620
That's why we need to continue the search!

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.500
You know that's not possible, Mrs. Spring.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:11.870
We've covered all of the searchable
parts of Planet McPa.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:15.120
"Quitterie and Funicia's mother
Olive Rafaeli"
We've covered all of the searchable
parts of Planet McPa.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:19.450
The only other places to look are
the ocean and very far offshore.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.950
It's simply hopeless.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:31.870
I don't believe they died
in the oceans of McPa.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:36.950
The boat was still docked,
engines not activated.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:40.790
Are you saying they all swam far into
the ocean? With all of their luggage?

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.080
Nothing makes sense.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:46.580
What other possibility is there?

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:47.950
Space.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:52.790
Space, did you say?

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:55.290
Don't you think it's possible?

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:58.160
How do you propose they went to space?

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:02.830
I don't know. Perhaps there was
a spaceship on Planet McPa...

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:04.750
That's stupid.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:09.790
"Kanata's father
Ray Hoshijima"
Absurd. Your argument is based on
a hypothetical spaceship and no evidence.

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:14.750
It would be just as strong an argument
to say there could have been two boats.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:18.290
In fact, that would be more convincing.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:24.450
No, I mean, it doesn't make sense that
no remains or luggage were found ashore!

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:28.950
If they're out in space, there's still
some chance that they're alive.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:30.160
Please search for them!

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.830
Mrs. Spring.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:36.870
I thought of something similar as well,

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:43.790
but the cost of such a search would be
staggering without government assistance.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.330
It simply isn't realistic.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.000
This is difficult for me, too.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.700
Difficult for all of us.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.910
As if my body is being torn apart.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.370
I'm sorry, I...

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.790
You are all in the same situation as I am.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:14.950
Don't mention it.
We all share the same sadness.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:18.080
Let's support each other.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.450
Speaking of the government...

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:26.450
Luca's father, Mr. Marco Esposito.
Is he not joining us today?

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:27.330
I believe he is a senator, is he not?

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:30.000
"Charce's mother
Sophie Lacroix"
I believe he is a senator, is he not?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.040
Perhaps he can talk to the government.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:37.200
He has done all of that, a long time ago.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:42.580
He told me that the government
cannot help us anymore.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:47.120
He's not with us because today
is the day of his DNA sampling.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:50.580
He was a leader of the faction opposing
the genome management project.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:55.910
I wonder how he feels about
getting his DNA sampled today.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.200
Senator Esposito!

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:01.620
What are your thoughts on completing
your DNA sampling?

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:01.950
"Luca's father
Marco Esposito"

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:04.750
"Luca's father
Marco Esposito"
I obey laws that are passed.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.120
"Luca's father
Marco Esposito"

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:09.410
What about the allegations
of illegal campaign donations?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.790
Your son is still missing!

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:14.000
Care to share your feelings?

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.330
It's as if my body is being torn apart.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.120
Please be safe...

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.080
Aries...

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.160
"Planet Arispade
Day 49 of being lost in space"

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:48.790
Here it comes!

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.000
Oops!

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.370
--Get it!
--Got it!

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.080
This planet is awesome!

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:16.580
Camp log, day 49 of being lost in space.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:23.580
We finally found land on this oceanic planet
and have spent five days on it.

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:30.660
Got one!

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:33.160
Got one!

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:35.080
Mine is bigger!

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.290
No, mine is!

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:38.910
--No, mine is!
--No, mine is!

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:39.540
--No, mine is!

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:41.830
--Did you make that harpoon?
--No, mine is!

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.330
I just shaved the tip a little.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:47.040
The Luca Javelin is easy to modify.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.830
I'm glad we brought a few along.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:52.790
Aren't you going to join them?

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:55.200
I told you, I can't swim.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.500
I got three today.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:02.410
Wow! Excellent marksmanship!

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:05.410
This bow is pretty good, Luca.

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.910
Can you tighten the string a little?

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:09.660
I'll make the adjustment.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.080
Guys!

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:15.870
We found more types of fruit!

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:17.160
Yummy!

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:18.250
Yummy.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:20.290
Yum, yum, yummy.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.540
Okay, all delicious.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.540
Let's go ahead and try them out.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.040
Here you are, my lady.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.790
Oh, how nice.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:38.410
Yes, delicious...

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.700
What's with all this peace?!

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.700
Whoa, what's this about?

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:46.830
It just struck me and
made me want to yell out!

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.500
What is this planet, some sort of paradise?!

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:54.250
It's practically a resort!
I don't really need to go home anymore!

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.330
Spending my days relaxing
with you all doesn't sound too bad!

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:57.910
She was so eager to get back.

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:01.830
This is such a departure from the tough
times we had, it's confusing her.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:06.160
Hey, where are Aries and Yunhua?

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.620
They said they were going to the lake.
Do you want to join them?

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.040
Hey!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.000
Quitterie! Funi!

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:26.950
Aries, you might not be aware of this,
but your swimsuit is pretty spicy.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:28.750
Huh?

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:32.700
I don't know if it's on purpose, but you've
got quite a sizable pair of breasts.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:37.830
You need to pay attention to your swimwear
or else you'll be targeted by boys!

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:43.040
All boys are idiots, remember that!

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.370
Quitterie, you're quite spicy too.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:53.200
No, I'm what they call "sexy."

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:59.750
Hey, what are you guys talking about?

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:02.450
Yunhua is quite spicy too.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:04.620
Enough already.

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:10.250
But Aries, if you approach him dressed
liked that, he should be easy to get.

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:11.620
Don't you think?

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:13.080
Huh?

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.370
I mean Kanata.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.410
What?!

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:25.620
I found something interesting
about the creatures on this planet.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.660
All of the creatures are parthenogenetic.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.620
Partheno-what?

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:33.500
They reproduce through cloning.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.700
That sounds really unique.

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.330
Not really.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:40.250
Some species of lizard, carp,
turkey, bees, dandelion...

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:43.500
Many known species are parthenogenetic.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:47.250
The females can reproduce by themselves.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:50.450
So there are no males on this planet?

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:54.790
It's possible, or it could be that we
simply haven't come across any yet.

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:56.080
I see.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:59.120
Seeing how so many species
coexist peacefully,

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:04.410
this could be a paradise resulting
from the ultimate evolution.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:09.950
Yeah, a world with no boys sure
sounds like paradise to me!

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.830
Right, Aries?!

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:14.870
Hey!

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:24.580
I understand you too well.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:28.200
Just be honest!
How do you feel about Kanata?

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:31.250
--How is it?!
--Quitterie is on the assault.

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:34.040
This is fun!

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.750
Kanata saved my life.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:39.290
It's only natural that I feel
positively about him.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:42.120
I suppose that could be how it started.

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.830
He's also kind of reliable after all.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:47.290
I guess falling in love was inevitable?

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:52.330
Oh... So cute!

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:56.700
You're usually so aloof and out there,
but so transparent when it comes to boys!

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:00.540
You're not hard to read either, Quitterie!

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:01.910
It's Zack, right?

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:04.000
Now Yunhua's on the assault?!

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:08.370
Huh?! I already told you.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:12.830
I just know him well
because we grew up together.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.540
Stop smirking! I've never seen
those expressions before!

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:20.500
So, what's your plan of attack?

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:21.750
Attack?

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:22.660
Confessing your feelings.

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:23.700
Whoa!

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:25.250
I'm not going to do that!

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:28.500
Well, maybe not right away.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:31.410
But who knows, Kanata could be
quite popular back home.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:35.830
Even I felt my heart skip a beat
when I saw his muscles.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:40.330
Maybe he already has a girlfriend.
You should ask.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:43.120
Quitterie looks so alive.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:44.290
So fun.

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:46.370
I'm not going to ask him that!

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:53.910
Hey, you want to use the washroom?

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:58.620
No, I, uh...

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:03.910
Kanata, you're like, uh...

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:08.160
At school, you're quite, um...

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:10.620
Uh... How to put this...

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:12.250
Are you popular with girls?!

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:12.870
Excuse me?

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:14.450
What a dumb way to ask!

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:20.790
Oh yeah, I'm mega popular.
Not just girls, but all humans!

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:23.410
He's no better. What a dumb response...

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:26.540
So then, um...

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:31.950
I was wondering if you, uh, had like,
a steady girlfriend or someone like that...

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:33.790
Good job, Aries! You did it!

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:36.620
Let it out, Kanata!

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:41.120
Of course! All women are my girl friends!

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:45.200
Wow, that's stupid. I've had enough.
What's wrong with him?

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:47.910
That's stupid.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:48.790
Huh?

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:52.290
Never mind. What's wrong with you?!

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:53.500
Huh...?

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.250
Stab!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:15.200
Team B5 camp log.
Planet Arispade day five.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:19.870
Due to personal reasons, I'm going to bed.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:28.410
"Planet Arispade
Day 50 of being lost in space"

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:39.370
Wow, six catches? Impressive!

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:44.200
I'm glad you can catch these birds.
There aren't any creatures on the ground.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:47.120
You've gotten better, Ulgar!

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.620
Hey, Ulgar. How's the bow?

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.040
Not bad.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:58.750
You got six of them?
You must have improved your skills.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.080
I did.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:03.660
I made a fishing rod.
Do you want to try it out?

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:04.910
I do.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:07.250
He won't talk to me.

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:09.500
Don't be jealous.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:13.000
Luca can get personal with anyone
without making a big deal about it.

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:14.330
I guess he's just easier to talk to.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:16.370
I'm easy to talk to, too.

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:18.000
You're actually just a bit annoying.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:24.080
Ulgar, do you have, like,
a favorite celebrity?

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:27.540
What do you do when you're alone?

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:30.200
Shut up.

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:35.080
How are you in school?
Do you have friends?

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:40.410
I don't make friends because
they're too much trouble. Like you!

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:43.370
You're just going to have to accept that.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:46.830
I don't plan on changing who I am.

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:48.830
Just like you.

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:50.040
Bah.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:57.410
Your dad is vice-principal, right?
What do you discuss at home?

00:18:57.410 --> 00:19:00.700
I rarely talk to my dad.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.790
I don't even consider him family.

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:05.620
Hmm.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:11.450
But seriously, I didn't realize your dad
was Mr. Zweig the vice-principal.

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:14.500
You'd think I'd notice, since you two
have the same last name, right?

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.620
Who even remembers
other people's last names?

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:22.120
I do. I remember everyone's full names.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:25.120
Ulgar, do you remember mine?

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:27.540
You should, since you're my friend now.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:30.250
I said I'm not your friend.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:32.040
It's Esposito.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:33.790
Luca Esposito.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:38.160
You don't have to remember
the others, I guess.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.830
Esposito?

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.450
Yes?

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:44.120
What does your father do?!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.120
He's a politician.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.910
I thought I told you...

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.950
Marco Esposito...

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:06.080
This is nice, everyone eating outside together.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:08.290
We're having a party today.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:09.910
More plates over there please.

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:12.870
So fun!

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:17.620
We were able to gather enough food
on this planet, thanks to you.

00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:19.500
We'll take off tomorrow.

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:23.950
I'm going to miss this place.
It's such a nice planet, it must be unique.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:26.950
I never thought I'd hear those
words from you, Quitterie.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:29.700
She said something about
wanting to live here for real.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:32.370
It really was quite a paradise.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:35.540
I never thought we'd have
such a relaxing time on this trip.

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.160
Yeah.

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:50.000
No matter how many photos we take,
we're not going to be able to save the feeling.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:53.290
Yes, seeing this first-hand while
experiencing the trip is quite different.

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:56.790
Looking back on a photo
would not be the same.

00:20:56.790 --> 00:21:01.410
I guess the experience is going
to fade away as we grow older.

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:03.540
That's a bit sad.

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:05.160
It doesn't have to be.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.950
My father is researching
memory transplant technology.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:12.500
You should know, your mother
helps with that research too.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:17.080
We might be able to save and
revisit memories in the near future.

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:19.160
That's not what I mean.

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.040
You really don't understand how
to think romantically, do you?

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:26.290
Zack's father and Quitterie's
mother work together.

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:32.500
Memories... Being like this makes us
forget what we're going through.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:41.000
Yeah, being thrown 5,000 light-years in space
as part of an assassination plot...

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.620
It's tough.

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:45.620
I almost forgot.

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:47.370
Don't remind her.

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:48.660
Sorry.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.750
But we're making good progress, right?

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:56.250
We got closer to the members
that were very shy at first.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:59.540
Our relationships are moving forward, too.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:06.660
Yeah! I don't really even believe
there's an enemy hiding amongst us!

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:19.200
Don't move.

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:21.000
Ulgar!

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:24.040
This is a real gun.

00:22:24.040 --> 00:22:26.910
Move, and I will shoot.

00:22:26.910 --> 00:22:32.290
No... Please tell me you're lying.

00:22:32.290 --> 00:22:35.870
Ulgar is the enemy...!
